{
  "id": "amplification-effect",
  "term": "amplification effect",
  "definition": "The amplification effect is the strengthening of a message’s framing effect when the information is presented in a more innovative form, such as visual graphics rather than plain text. In this study, that stronger impact was seen in people’s risk perception, positive emotion, and willingness to help, especially when the information was encountered in real time.",
